mw2coop patch for maps/_coop.gsc (Modern Warfare 2, 64-bit Steam build)

1. Revive prompt: Spec Ops gives players body models (SetModelFunc), campaign levels do not,
   so a campaign player has a model index but no DObj and linkTo( player, "tag_origin" )
   raises a script error (link builtin @0x18ff30, "parent has no dobj" path). That ends the
   downed thread before the revive prompt, HUD and bleed-out timer exist. Link to the player
   entity itself instead (no tag) in a co-op campaign session.
2. A downed player who bleeds out (or both down) is killed here, which in Spec Ops ends the
   mission. In the campaign the mission is failed and restarted at the checkpoint by
   maps\_mw2coop::mission_failed() instead; kill() would also fail on a player it has already
   made invulnerable.
3. Spec Ops never gets past player_coop_kill() in player_coop_downed(): the player dies and the
   thread ends on "death". In the campaign the player lives on, so stop there once the level
   has ended; otherwise the revive prompt and bleed-out HUD start after their cleanup ran.
@@@ replace
	level.revive_ent linkTo( self, "tag_origin" );
@@@ with
	if ( maps\_mw2coop::is_campaign_coop() )
		level.revive_ent linkTo( self );
	else
		level.revive_ent linkTo( self, "tag_origin" );
@@@ end
@@@ replace
	if ( flag( "coop_fail_when_all_dead" ) )
		flag_wait( "coop_alldowned" );

@@@ with
	if ( flag( "coop_fail_when_all_dead" ) )
		flag_wait( "coop_alldowned" );

	if ( maps\_mw2coop::is_campaign_coop() )
	{
		level thread maps\_mw2coop::mission_failed();
		return;
	}

@@@ end
@@@ replace
		self player_coop_kill();

	self player_coop_create_use_target();
@@@ with
		self player_coop_kill();

	if ( maps\_mw2coop::is_campaign_coop() && flag( "special_op_terminated" ) )
		return;

	self player_coop_create_use_target();
@@@ end
@@@ replace
		self player_coop_kill();

	self player_coop_set_original_attributes();
@@@ with
		self player_coop_kill();

	if ( maps\_mw2coop::is_campaign_coop() && flag( "special_op_terminated" ) )
		return;

	self player_coop_set_original_attributes();
@@@ end
